1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
How AI reads — it can't see letters

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,200
Part 1 of 2: CHUNKS

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,800
Watch it learn to read. It glues the most common pair, over and over.

4
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,200
s t r a w b e r r y  →  s t r a w b-er r y  →  s t r a w ber r y

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,600
→ s t r a w berr y  →  s t r a w berry  →  st ra w berry  →  straw berry

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,200
Nobody told it “straw” or “berry” — it just counted

7
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,400
3 r's.  2 chunks.  So ask it to count the r's and watch.

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,000
Part 2 of 2: THREADS

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
the animal didn't cross the street because it was too tired

10
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,000
Which one is “it”?

11
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
The animal — 85%. Because tired is a thing animals are.

12
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,000
Change ONE word at the end: “because it was too wide”

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,400
And the link jumps — now “it” is the street

14
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,000
It never reads a word. It reads the pieces, and the links.

15
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Pause. Observe. Learn.  Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
